📝 Technical Questions

What is a Test Plan?
A test plan is a document that defines what to test, how to test, and who will do it. 
Its purpose is to make sure testing is organized, complete, and efficient. 
It usually includes the scope, objectives, approach, environment, roles, and schedule. 
For example, if I were testing a login module, the plan would cover valid and invalid logins, 
password recovery, tools, timelines, and responsibilities, so nothing is missed.


